            "currentUpdate": "The founder reviews the operative decision recorded during his outside admission for a perforated sigmoid primary with unresectable liver and lung metastases. Before admission he requested treatment of reversible acute complications. At the recorded decision point, the perforated sigmoid segment had been resected and the remaining bowel ends were viable. Diffuse fecal contamination had been encountered. Despite fluids, antibiotics and resection, norepinephrine was still required and the bowel was edematous. The operative team judged fascial closure feasible without a planned open abdomen.",
            "stem": "At that outside intraoperative decision point, which reconstruction plan best fits {patientName}'s recorded findings?",
            "answerChoices": [
              {
                "id": "choice.cpc.perforation-overrides-systemic-first.hartmann.v2",
                "label": "Close the rectal stump and create an end colostomy",
                "isCorrect": true,
                "rationale": "Ongoing vasopressor need with fecal contamination and edematous bowel favors avoiding a new colorectal anastomosis. A concrete Hartmann reconstruction is supported here; no universal rule for every perforation is asserted.",
                "serviceRequest": null
              },
              {
                "id": "choice.cpc.perforation-overrides-systemic-first.protected.v2",
                "label": "Create a colorectal anastomosis and a diverting loop ileostomy",
                "isCorrect": false,
                "rationale": "Diversion does not remove an anastomosis or its failure risk. The continuing vasopressor need and adverse local conditions favor not constructing it at this recorded point.",
                "serviceRequest": null
              },
              {
                "id": "choice.cpc.perforation-overrides-systemic-first.unprotected.v2",
                "label": "Create a colorectal anastomosis without proximal diversion",
                "isCorrect": false,
                "rationale": "The relevant observations are the current vasopressor need, contamination and edema, not earlier cancer-treatment eligibility.",
                "serviceRequest": null
              }
            ],
