            "currentUpdate": "A completed biofeedback course is documented. Current manometry shows anal relaxation during bearing down, and balloon expulsion meets laboratory criteria. The returned contrast-evacuation study shows material retained in an anterior rectal pouch after the rest of the rectum empties; vaginal pressure releases it. Soft-stool evacuation still requires splinting and limits daily activities.",
