            "currentUpdate": "The original CT showed a ureteral stone with upstream dilation, and the stone was also identifiable on the baseline abdominal radiograph. At the planned trial-of-passage review he reports that pain stopped after passing gritty material into the toilet. He did not recover material for inspection. Creatinine is at baseline and he is afebrile.",
