            "currentUpdate": "During the outside admission, a purulent subcutaneous incisional pocket was opened and decompressed, and piperacillin-tazobactam was administered. Across the examinations before that procedure and at the recorded reassessment, {patientName}'s fever and deep left pelvic pain persisted while incisional pain and redness diminished. Blood pressure was maintained without vasopressors, and tenderness remained confined to the lower abdomen without generalized guarding. The CT report obtained at that reassessment is shown below. Antibacterial therapy and incisional wound care continued under all plans.",
