                "rationale": "Improvement at the opened incision does not establish drainage of the pelvic compartment. The persisting deep symptoms and the fluid, debris and inflammatory findings in a different compartment support an unaddressed focal infection. Its confined distribution, the examination and the reported access anatomy favor image-guided drainage while antibacterial care continues. Failure to demonstrate contrast escape does not exclude an occult communication; deterioration or diffuse contamination would require renewed operative assessment.",
